OVERVIEW: Check study completeness: series and instance counts, and gaps in
Instance Number (0020,0013)

A gap in Instance Number (0020,0013) within a series is reported as missing.
This is a heuristic: PS3.3 Table C.7-9 defines Instance Number as "A number
that identifies this image" (Type 2) and does not require consecutive numbering.

USAGE: dicom-study check <path> [--expected-series <expected-series>] [--expected-instances <expected-instances>] [--report <report>] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <path>                  Study directory

OPTIONS:
  --expected-series <expected-series>
                          Expected number of series in the study (Number of
                          Study Related Series)
  --expected-instances <expected-instances>
                          Expected number of instances in each series (Number
                          of Series Related Instances)
  --report <report>       Output report file path
  -v, --verbose           Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

